Cause (levi/src/facts.rs): CommitFacts are gated by the facts-published cache, but RefFacts are built unconditionally for every refs/heads/* on every run, and each carries observed = now(). So a repo with N branches appends N events to the hub log on EVERY sync ‚Äî and since opportunistic sync fires after every mutation, that is unbounded growth for an idle repo. It is also immune to hub-side ingest dedupe (lv-5f11): the observed timestamp makes each event a genuinely distinct payload, so the dedupe there cannot collapse them.

Same event-log-bloat class as the 2026-07-21 flood, just slow instead of catastrophic: pulse-deploy alone writes 95 events per sync indefinitely.

